-- ============================================================================
-- H3 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Process Safety: LOPA & SIL Determination, beginner
-- tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/lopa/beginner.
--
-- What this tier owns: HOW MUCH RISK REDUCTION IS MISSING. A LOPA row is one
-- initiating event frequency times its enabling conditions and conditional
-- modifiers; an IPL is credited once, and only when flagged independent and
-- not flagged unauditable; the required risk reduction factor is the mitigated
-- frequency over the TMEL and the required PFDavg is its reciprocal, the
-- binding target; six outcome states; the low demand bands; an exact decade
-- belongs to the lower SIL, and the engine snaps within one part in a billion;
-- and one worksheet end to end, with the risk matrix seam. Digest sections 1
-- to 13, and section 32.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A band is a label and the required PFDavg is
-- the target. The Associate capstone grades frequencies, a required RRF, a
-- required PFDavg, the loop through a proposed SIF and an exact decade, and
-- grades no PFDavg computed from failure rates.
-- ============================================================================

